    // Sales Pipeline
    'sales_pipeline' => 'Sales Pipeline',
    'sales_pipeline_desc' => 'Track and manage sales opportunities through customizable pipeline stages for revenue forecasting.',
    'kanban_intro' => 'Invent-MAG is using the Kanban methodology to help you visualize and manage your sales pipeline. What is Kanban? Kanban is a visual method for managing work across different stages. Think of it like a whiteboard with sticky notes - each note represents an opportunity, and you move it from one column to another as progress is made.',
    'step1_pipeline' => 'Step 1 - Create Pipeline: Click "Manage Pipelines" → "Add New Pipeline" tab to create your first pipeline. Give it a name (e.g., "Sales Pipeline 2024"), description, and optionally set it as default.',
    'step2_pipeline' => 'Step 2 - Configure Stages: In the "Manage Pipelines" modal, go to the "Pipelines" tab and click the edit button on your pipeline. Use the stage form to add stages (e.g., Lead, Contacted, Quoted, Won, Lost). Mark stages as "Closed" if they are final stages like Won or Lost.',
    'step3_pipeline' => 'Step 3 - Create Opportunities: Once your pipeline has stages, click the "+" button to create new opportunities. Select the customer, add products, set estimated value, expected close date, and notes.',
    'kanban_board' => 'Kanban Board: View opportunities as cards organized by pipeline stages. Drag and drop cards to move them between stages to update their progress.',
    'edit_pipeline_info' => 'Edit Pipeline Info: Click the edit button on a pipeline card in the "Pipelines" tab to modify its name, description, or default status.',
    'edit_delete_pipeline' => 'Edit & Delete: Choose the edit button or delete button on each opportunity card to edit details or delete the opportunity from the pipeline.',
    'convert_sales' => 'Convert to Sales: Click the convert button on Won opportunities to transform them into actual sales orders for fulfillment.',

